From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:34:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: max77759: zero the regulator and power supply
 configs

max77759_charger_probe() fills in only some fields of its struct
regulator_config and struct power_supply_config, both on the stack.
The remaining fields (init_data, regmap, ena_gpiod, attr_grp,
supplied_to, ...) are then whatever the stack held, unless the kernel
happens to be built with CONFIG_INIT_STACK_ALL_ZERO.

Zero-initialise both.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/max77759_charger.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/max77759_charger.c b/drivers/power/supply/max77759_charger.c
index 689fc733f..5fb2bffa0 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/max77759_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/max77759_charger.c
@@ -683,8 +683,8 @@ static void max_tcpci_unregister_psy_notifier(void *nb)
 
 static int max77759_charger_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
-	struct regulator_config chgin_otg_reg_cfg;
-	struct power_supply_config psy_cfg;
+	struct regulator_config chgin_otg_reg_cfg = { };
+	struct power_supply_config psy_cfg = { };
 	struct device *dev = &pdev->dev;
 	struct max77759_charger *chg;
 	int ret;
